  31:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****         /**
  32:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          * When sending MIDI messages immediately back-to-back in user code,
  33:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          * sometimes the USB CDC driver is still "busy".
  34:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          *
  35:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          * This option configures the number of times to retry a Tx after
  36:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          * delaying for 100 microseconds (default = 3 retries).
  37:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          *
  38:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          * If you set this to zero, Tx will not retry so the attempt will block
  39:../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy/src/hid/usb_midi.h ****          * for slightly less time, but transmit can fail if the Tx state is busy.
